 link, and %s for the query string\n\n* https://www.google.com/search?q=%s&udm=14\n\n---\nScreenshot of Gemini spilling beans\n\nhttps://files.catbox.moe/dudvvv.jpg", "author": "5DchessWatch", "created": 1785767928195, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "JoePlumber", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Google's AI Gemini spilled the beans on a secret setting that lets you go back to traditional search without the AI summary", "last_comment_created": 1785768667235, "content": "<p>You add the &quot;&amp;udm=14&quot; to the end of your query and it will go back to normal pre AI summary google with traditional results</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Example</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=test&amp;udm=14\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.google.com/search?q=test&amp;udm=14</a></li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>So in brave/chrome you add a new search engine because you can't mod the original google search engine entry.  I did 'goog2' and then put in the above link, and %s for the query string</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=%s&amp;udm=14\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.google.com/search?q=%s&amp;udm=14</a></li>\n</ul>\n<hr />\n<p>Screenshot of Gemini spilling beans</p>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://files.catbox.moe/dudvvv.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://files.catbox.moe/dudvvv.jpg</a></p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 4, "score_up": 8, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "DEPORT", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locke